<.shell title="Top bar" current={:top_bar}>
  <h1>Top bar</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Navy, with the amber rule and logo. It holds the main sections and the account menu.
  </p>

  <div class="demo bar-demo" style="padding: 0">
    <Web.Layouts.main_nav_bar
      current_user={sample_user()}
      current_team={sample_team()}
      current_path="/teams/squamish/activities"
    />
  </div>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The current section is underlined in amber.</li>
    <li>
      The account menu is a short list under a button. Keep menus for a few links that don't fit in the bar. Actions on a page are buttons.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>On a phone</h3>
  <p>
    Below 1024px the sections, Admin, and the account menu move behind a Menu button. The
    panel opens under the amber rule, the width of the screen, with the current section
    marked in amber. Going to another page closes it.
  </p>
  <div class="demo phone-width phone-bar-demo" style="padding: 0">
    <Web.Layouts.main_nav_bar
      current_user={sample_user()}
      current_team={sample_team()}
      current_path="/teams/squamish/activities"
    />
  </div>
  <script>
    // Open the menus, so the examples show them.
    document.querySelectorAll(".bar-demo .site-bar-menu, .phone-bar-demo .site-bar-phone")
      .forEach(function (menu) { menu.open = true; });
  </script>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    The layout's <code>main_nav_bar</code>, built from <code>&lt;.site_bar&gt;</code>. The menus are open here so you can see them.
  </p>
</.shell>
